NOTE ON WHAT THE 13 COVERS. The gate walks every `## T-NNN` section in tasks.md.
T-001..T-012 are `Status: Done`, which is the state that additionally demands a
verification/<task-id>.evidence.json bundle and forces the gate to revalidate
each task's contract, its bundle, and the bundle's declared quality-gate report
(check-task-state.sh:5-12) - that is why twelve contract/bundle pairs are
re-verified above rather than merely counted. T-013 is `Status: Implementation
Complete`, whose only additional requirement is an implementation report
mentioning the task id (check-task-state.sh:13); that report is
reports/implementation/epic-189-a1-project-context/T-013.md.

THIS RUN DELIBERATELY OBSERVES T-013 AS `Implementation Complete`, NOT AS `Done`.
Recording `Status: Done` is the main session's job and is explicitly outside this
chain's scope. `git diff --cached -- specs/epic-189-a1-project-context/tasks.md`
was re-checked immediately before this chain's commit and is EMPTY; tasks.md is
not among the paths this commit stages.

THE "dirty working tree" WARNINGS ARE HISTORICAL, NOT THIS ROUND'S. They are
emitted from each task's own stored bundle, recording the tree state at the time
THAT bundle was generated; they are not a statement about the tree now. The
working tree at this run was clean - `git status --porcelain` produced no output
immediately before this invocation, and again after the 25 individual suite runs
recorded in regression.log. The pattern also matches the T-011 and T-012 chains
exactly: T-007 and T-009 carry no warning, every other Done task does.

THE GATE IS NOT VACUOUS HERE. It is the same binary that returns non-zero on a
missing bundle or a failing contract; this round exercised that path
independently, because `bash plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-contract.sh`
run against T-013's own contract is recorded separately in this chain and had to
be made to pass on its own terms (medium tier, acceptance-first) before this
output could be produced.
